<Page
  route="about"
  title="About"
  heading="About"
  description="Neura Mobilis, a start-up founded by four AI students, builds AI that restores autonomy and mobility to people with spinal cord injuries."
  lead="Four artificial intelligence students, equal partners, brought together by one idea: using AI to give people back their autonomy."
>
  <h2>Why we do this</h2>
  <p>
    A spinal cord injury often affects young people. Thanks to the plasticity of the nervous system,
    some capacity for recovery remains one to two years after the injury. But state-of-the-art equipment
    is expensive, rare and available for short sessions, in only a few centres.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    We started by listening. The team of a rehabilitation centre, including a physiotherapist, and two
    people with tetraplegia described their daily life and the limits of current solutions. Mobilis came
    out of these conversations, and our testers decide what comes next.
  </p>
  <p>The project is supported by our school's incubator. The company is being set up.</p>

  <h2>Write to us</h2>
  <p>
    To test Mobilis, work with us or simply learn more: <a href={routes.tester.en}>become a tester</a> or
    write to us at the address at the bottom of the page.
  </p>
</Page>
